---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { roadmapCheckedAgainst } from '../data/app';
---
<Base title="Roadmap" checked={roadmapCheckedAgainst}>
  <div class="page">
    <div>
      <h1>What comes next?</h1>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>These are the changes planned for Sudo Hire after v1.1.0. Nothing here has a date. When a change is released, it leaves this list, and the other pages describe it.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>An About section in Settings.</strong> It shows the app version, for example “Sudo Hire 1.0.1”. Today the version is only in Get Info in Finder and in the diagnostic report.</li>
        <li><strong>One update notification, in the words of the app.</strong> When a new version is ready, only this notification shows: “Sudo Hire 1.1.0 is ready. It installs when you quit Sudo Hire.”</li>
        <li><strong>A keyword that matches only a tag needs a developer title.</strong> Today a keyword matches the title or the tags of a job. Some employers add tags for technologies that the job does not use, for example “php” on a job for an office assistant. Since v1.0.2, the list row says where the keyword matched, for example “Matched "php" in the tags from Remotive”, but the job still shows. After the change, a job that matches only in its tags also needs a developer role in its title, for example developer, engineer or programmer. A match in the title works as today.</li>
        <li><strong>Two more career page providers: SmartRecruiters and BambooHR.</strong> Today Sudo Hire reads Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Personio and Workable. This is not decided yet.</li>
        <li><strong>A new company shows when it is read.</strong> Sudo Hire reads the career pages at most every 6 hours. A company that you add shows “Next scan”, but it can wait up to 6 hours for its first read. After the change, Sudo Hire reads a new company at the next scan, or shows the real time, for example “Next read at 23:55”.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
